{number: 86}
{title: Jesus, Saviour, Pilot Me}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] Jesus, Savior, [Eb] pilot [Bb] me
Over life's tem-[F7] pestuous [Bb] sea;
Unknown waves be-[Eb] fore me [Bb] roll,
Hiding rock and [F7] treacherous [Bb] shoal;
Chart and compass [Eb] come from [Bb] Thee,
Jesus, Savior, [F7] pilot [Bb] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Bb] As a mother [Eb] stills her [Bb] child,
Thou canst hush the [F7] ocean [Bb] wild;
Boisterous waves o-[Eb] bey Thy [Bb] will
When Thou biddest [F7] to them "Be [Bb] still."
Wondrous sovereign [Eb] of the [Bb] sea,
Jesus, Savior, [F7] pilot [Bb] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Bb] When at last I [Eb] near the [Bb] shore,
And the fearful [F7] breakers [Bb] roar
'Twixt me and the [Eb] peaceful [Bb] land,
Still supported [F7] by Thy [Bb] hand,
May I hear Thee [Eb] say to [Bb] me,
"Fear not, I will [F7] pilot [Bb] thee."
{end_of_verse}
